  id: W2_C
  era: c. 400 CE
  title: The Iron Pillar of Delhi (replica)
  text: The Iron Pillar of Delhi (replica). This towering column was forged from wrought iron about 1,600 years ago and weighs some six tonnes. A Sanskrit inscription honours a king named Chandra, usually identified as the Gupta emperor Chandragupta II. Now in the Qutb complex in Delhi, the pillar has barely rusted, thanks to a thin protective film rich in phosphorus. Forging a single iron object this large was an extraordinary achievement for its time. Metallurgists still study the pillar to understand how its rust-resistant surface formed.
  narration: {fileID: 8300000, guid: 9fe21b805daee4324a016e3d9284580d, type: 3}
